<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n62907" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῆμμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαμβάνω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>anything received</i>, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόμα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Antig.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.182e
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. καὶ ἀνάλωμα</span>
			<i>receipt</i> and expense, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				32.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				920c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Anaxandr.
				26
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνενεγκεῖν </span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν</span>- Pap.) <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν
				λήμματι</span> place to <i>credit,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PEleph.
				15.4
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				1346.2
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B.C.)</span>, etc.: generally, <i>gain, profit</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				5.12
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. τι κέρδους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					45.14
				</span></i>
			; esp. of <i>unjust gain</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Din.
				1.45
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παντὸς ἥττων λήμματος</span>
			unable to resist any temptation <i>of gain</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				19.339
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥσπερ ἂν τρυτάνη ἐπὶ τὸ λ. ῥέπειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					18.298
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. λαβεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					21.28
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				27.39
			</span></i>: freq. in pl., <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				313
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				8.25
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ λ. τοῦ ἀργυρίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					49.57
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λημμάτων μετέχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					58.40
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τἀπὸ Θρᾴκης λ. ἕλκουσι δεῦρο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antiph.
					196
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in Logic,
				<i>statement taken</i> as true, <i>assumption</i>; esp.
				<i>premiss</i> in a syllogism, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ λ. τῷ τοιούτῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.D.
					<u>Synt.</u>
					245.13
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ οἰκεῖα τῇ ἐπιστήμῃ λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Top.</u>
					101a14
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λήμματα τιθέναι</span> ib. <i><span class="en">
				156a21
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gell.
				9.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1.9
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>; prop. <i>the major premiss</i> (the minor being <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόσληψις</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Crinis
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				3.269
			</span></i>; later, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποδεικτικὰ λήμματα
				παρασχεῖν</span> offer scientific <i>proofs</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.627
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>matter, substance</i>, or <i>argument</i> of a sentence,
			etc., opp. form or style (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέξις</span>), <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Dem.</u>
				20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Longin.
				15.10
			</span></i>, etc.: hence, <i>title</i> or <i>argument</i> of an
			epigram, Lat. <i>lemma</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Mart.
				14.2
			</span></i>; <i>theme</i> or <i>thesis</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				4.27.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Mart.
				10.59
			</span></i>; <i>nutricis lemmata</i>, 'baby songs', <i><span class="en">
				Aus.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				12.90
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b> in <i><span class="en">
				LXX
			</span></i>, <i>burden</i> laid on one, <i>commission received</i>,
			esp. of <i>prophecy, Na.</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				1.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Je.</u>
				23.33
			</span></i>, al.; even, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῆμμα ἰδεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Hb.</u>
					1.1
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>La.</u>
				2.14
			</span></i>.</div>
